   "design": "Job ads start from the restaurant's earlier ads in the applicant tracking system ({ATS}), and applications arrive there with a few fixed questions (availability, hygiene certificate), sorted but never rejected automatically; the chef reads every application. Once the chef has picked candidates, they get a link to book an interview or trial shift. Interviews and the hiring decision stay with the chef.",
   "previous_blocker": "Applications came by e-mail and interviews were arranged by phone.",
   "enabler_now": "Applicant tracking systems hold ads, screening questions and self-booking links.",
   "still_hard": "Good cooks show themselves in a trial shift, not on paper.",
   "human_edge": "Seeing in a trial shift who keeps calm when the tickets pile up.",
